    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster, as his elite 81.88 score against Alcantara stands out as our primary engine for counting stats. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup and a dynamic platoon advantage that elevates his floor. Meanwhile, the optimizer is high on the offensive ceiling for **Josh Lowe** (68.69) and **Miguel Vargas** (66.48). Despite hitting 9th, **Josh Lowe** is a priority play due to a soft matchup against Fedde and his elite speed profile, which gains a 2% efficiency boost from the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014an essential factor in our pursuit of stolen bases. **Miguel Vargas** similarly capitalizes on a high-upside matchup against Aldegheri, where his platoon edge and the opposing pitcher's 5.50 xERA suggest a prime opportunity to drive in runs.\n\nRegarding roster management, the most difficult decision involved keeping **Marcell Ozuna** (61.17) on the bench. While his score is robust and exceeds several active starters, he was squeezed out by the high-ceiling profiles of **Heliot Ramos** (62.23) and **Josh Jung** (64.67), both of whom are projected for more favorable situational outcomes today. **Heliot Ramos** remains a tactical inclusion due to his speed profile against a pitcher with slow delivery, reinforcing our commitment to the SB category even at the cost of sitting a high-floor bat like **Marcell Ozuna**. \n\nWe are closely monitoring the risks associated with **Jacob Wilson**, whose score of 50.93 is hampered by a significant -19% penalty due to the high skill level of S\u00e1nchez. While his leadoff position provides volume, he is essentially a marginal start. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 48.73 reflects a tough matchup against Kirby. While our depth is tested by these matchups, the potential for high-impact production from **Kyle Tucker** and **Nolan Schanuel** should help stabilize our daily output as we look to navigate the current scarcity in stolen bases.",
